Subject: Join shader compilation and retire Vulkan resources before process exit

Shader-thread join adapted from ThomasEricB's BSD-2-Clause fix:
https://github.com/ThomasEricB/gamescope-lanczos-downscaling/commit/2e9a5a5fb3f3d7bfaf84c9f2341f5695d059b62b

Reproduced on RTX 5090 / NVIDIA 615.78.08 after a short Vulkan client exits.
First gamescope-shdr crashes in the driver's compiler. After joining it,
CVulkanCmdBuffer's static destructor calls FreeCommandBuffers through an
unloaded ICD. Release command buffers, ReShade and output textures after
the compositor threads finish, before dynamic-library exit handlers run.
No renderer, format, fence, or presentation behavior changes.

diff --git a/src/main.cpp b/src/main.cpp
index 6a0fdb1..39b2d60 100644
--- a/src/main.cpp
+++ b/src/main.cpp
@@ -1115,6 +1115,7 @@ int main(int argc, char **argv)
 
 	gamescope::Process::KillAllChildren( getpid(), SIGTERM );
 	gamescope::Process::WaitForAllChildren();
+	vulkan_release_shutdown_resources();
 }
 
